00:54:59.540 --> 00:55:02.880
And Isabel was already really familiar with the hair and makeup trailer.

1278
00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:08.200
So, she was actually very excited that she got to sit in the chair and not just pop in and say hi to me.

1279
00:55:08.200 --> 00:55:16.100
Well, what I loved about our hair and makeup folks, Angela, is that, you know, these little girls didn't really need hair and makeup.

1280
00:55:16.360 --> 00:55:16.540
No.

1281
00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:18.380
But they fussed over them.

1282
00:55:18.500 --> 00:55:18.920
Yes.

1283
00:55:19.100 --> 00:55:20.420
They made it an event.

1284
00:55:20.700 --> 00:55:23.660
This day was like a whole event for these little girls.

1285
00:55:23.860 --> 00:55:28.700
So, they would like maybe put their hair in a ponytail or pigtails or something, but they would linger.

1286
00:55:29.060 --> 00:55:29.340
Yeah.

1287
00:55:29.500 --> 00:55:32.880
And they would brush their faces even if there wasn't any makeup on it.

1288
00:55:32.940 --> 00:55:34.620
It was the cutest thing.

1289
00:55:34.820 --> 00:55:35.580
It was so cute.

1290
00:55:35.580 --> 00:55:41.180
In fact, one time Isabel was on set, and I think I've shared this before, and I think my forehead was shiny.

1291
00:55:41.420 --> 00:55:43.460
They said, Angela, you have a little bit of shine.

1292
00:55:43.600 --> 00:55:45.380
And they powdered my forehead.

1293
00:55:46.140 --> 00:55:51.220
So, Isabel walked into the hair and makeup, and she said to Sherry, can I get a little shine?

1294
00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:51.760
Yeah.

1295
00:55:52.020 --> 00:55:53.740
Because she thought that was what you got.

1296
00:55:54.220 --> 00:55:54.620
Yes.

1297
00:55:54.620 --> 00:56:00.200
And they just put their hair up in little ponytails, and then, you know, they got a tiny little bit of chapstick.

1298
00:56:00.480 --> 00:56:00.760
Yes.

1299
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:01.980
And a little bit of shine.

1300
00:56:02.720 --> 00:56:03.520
So sweet.

1301
00:56:04.060 --> 00:56:08.700
Well, the location of this recital was the 20th Century Women's Club in Eagle Rock.

1302
00:56:08.940 --> 00:56:15.100
And I asked Steve Burgess, what was involved on the production end when you have a bunch of little kids on set?

1303
00:56:15.120 --> 00:56:17.040
Because I know they can only work certain hours.

1304
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:18.140
They have to have breaks.

1305
00:56:18.380 --> 00:56:19.600
They have to have tutors.

1306
00:56:19.720 --> 00:56:21.320
They have to have a parent or guardian.

1307
00:56:22.020 --> 00:56:27.040
Steve said, since these were just three- and four-year-olds, they didn't really have to go to school.

1308
00:56:27.040 --> 00:56:32.720
But they did have a school teacher there because it's required by California law.

1309
00:56:32.840 --> 00:56:34.740
But they didn't really make them go to school.

1310
00:56:34.860 --> 00:56:36.760
And that the shooting was very short.

1311
00:56:37.060 --> 00:56:38.320
It was very short.

1312
00:56:38.320 --> 00:56:42.060
