1376
00:59:43.320 --> 00:59:46.340
My question is, why is there all of a sudden a boom operator?

1377
00:59:46.660 --> 00:59:53.100
They've had lapel mics this whole time, and out of nowhere, there's a boom operator who's been doing sound for Pam this whole time.

1378
00:59:53.940 --> 01:00:01.140
Well, Lindsay, I think this was something that, like, we knew as actors are making a show,

1379
01:00:01.280 --> 01:00:05.620
which is that you wear a mic pack and you have a boom operator.

1380
01:00:05.620 --> 01:00:07.620
It's very common to have both.

1381
01:00:07.820 --> 01:00:14.540
They want to have backup sound, and so they grab sound in two different ways on projects.

1382
01:00:14.880 --> 01:00:15.400
Always.

1383
01:00:15.580 --> 01:00:15.820
Always.

1384
01:00:16.060 --> 01:00:16.280
Always.

1385
01:00:16.560 --> 01:00:22.080
Even when Josh and I do our little baking videos at home, we have a lav mic kit that we bought,

1386
01:00:22.100 --> 01:00:24.280
so we put the little mics on our shirts.

1387
01:00:24.560 --> 01:00:26.740
But then he has one boom mic.

1388
